---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const updated = 'August 2026';
const supportEmail = 'yash@typethink.ai';
---

<AppLayout
	title="Terms of Service — doodleai.art"
	description="The terms for using doodleai.art, a bring-your-own-key doodle generation chat tool with no accounts."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
			<h1>Terms of <span class="grad">Service</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Plain language, no tricks. doodleai.art is a free, bring-your-own-key tool — these terms
				explain what that means for you.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

			<h2>What this site is</h2>
			<p>
				doodleai.art lets you chat with an agent to turn a photo (or a described character) into
				a hand-drawn doodle image, using your own PicX API key for generation. It is
				<strong>a side project</strong>, provided as-is.
			</p>

			<h2>No account needed</h2>
			<p>
				There is no sign up, no login, and no password. You bring your own PicX API key, which is
				stored only in your browser's local storage — we never see it, and we don't associate
				anything you generate with an identity.
			</p>

			<h2>It's free to use</h2>
			<p>
				Using doodleai.art costs nothing — there's no subscription or payment to us. Generation
				itself runs through your own PicX API key and the chat runs on a model via OpenRouter, so
				any usage costs beyond their free tiers are between you and them, not us.
			</p>

			<h2>Your photos and doodles</h2>
			<p>
				You keep whatever rights you have in any photo you attach and any doodle that's generated
				from it. Attaching a photo sends it to PicX (under your own key) so it can be processed —
				don't attach a photo you don't have the right to use. Doodles you generate, your saved
				moodboard, and any "characters" (saved reference photos) you create stay in your own browser
				unless you export or delete them yourself.
			</p>

			<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Keep it your own.</b> Don't attach photos or images you don't have the right to use.</li>
				<li><b>No harassment or impersonation.</b> Don't use the tool to target, shame, or impersonate someone without consent.</li>
				<li><b>No automation or abuse.</b> Don't script, scrape, or flood the app's endpoints.</li>
				<li><b>No illegal or harmful content.</b> Don't use the site for anything unlawful, hateful, or explicit.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We can block abusive traffic at our discretion, without notice.
			</p>

			<h2>Third-party services</h2>
			<p>
				Generation and photo hosting run through <a href="https://picxstudio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PicX</a>
				under your own API key; the chat agent runs on a model routed through
				<a href="https://openrouter.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenRouter</a>. Your
				use of those services through this site is also subject to their own terms.
			</p>

			<h2>No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				The site is provided as is. There is no guarantee it stays online or that any given
				generation succeeds.
			</p>

			<h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
			<p>
				To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from your use of the
				site. This is a side project — please treat it as one.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms may change. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
				updated version.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions or complaints:
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Back to the app</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
